        "heading": "Methodology & Technical Formulation",
        "content": "Our proposed methodology formulates an empirical framework evaluated over rigorous benchmark datasets. Specifically, While Multi-Version Concurrency Control (MVCC) prevents readers from blocking writers, accumulating dead tuples and outdated version chains leads to severe cache thrashing. We analyze version storage strategies—append-only, time-travel, and rollback segments—evaluating epoch-based and cooperative garbage collection in high-concurrency systems. We establish formal invariant boundaries, prove algorithmic convergence criteria, and enforce robust transactional validation throughout iterative executions."
